<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  MindForge's privacy manifest.

  Every array here is empty, and each one is empty for a reason the repository
  can be checked against rather than for a reason we assert:

  - NSPrivacyTracking / NSPrivacyTrackingDomains — there is no network code in
    this app at all. dependency_policy_test fails the build if http, dio, a
    websocket client, an analytics SDK or a crash reporter enters the tree, so
    there is nothing that could contact a domain, let alone track across apps.

  - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes — nothing is collected because nothing leaves
    the device. Runs and settings live in one SQLite file in the app's own
    container; the only exit path the product has is a user-initiated export.

  - NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes — the app calls no required-reason API itself.
    The one plugin that could, path_provider_foundation, ships its OWN manifest
    declaring an empty NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes array, so there is nothing to
    transcribe from it. This list is copied from the Pods' manifests when there
    is something to copy — it is never reasoned about, because a wrong reason
    code is an App Review rejection rather than a compile error.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
